# My Budget Tracker – Visual Identity

## Project Description
My Budget Tracker is a simple web application designed to help users track their expenses and manage their daily spending.

## Week 3 – Visual Design Challenge

This week, I improved the visual identity of my existing Budget Tracker using CSS.

## Features and Design Improvements

### 1. Color Palette
- Blue for buttons and table headers.
- Light grey for the page background.
- White for content cards.
- Dark navy for headings.

### 2. Typography
- Merriweather for headings.
- Open Sans for body text, forms, and tables.
- Google Fonts used to improve readability.

### 3. Table and Form Styling
- Styled input fields and dropdown menus.
- Added padding and borders to table cells.
- Added alternating row colors.
- Styled buttons with hover effects.

### 4. CSS Box Model
- Used margin to separate sections.
- Used padding to create internal spacing.
- Added borders and rounded corners.
- Used box shadows to distinguish content cards.

## Technologies Used
- HTML5
- CSS3
- Google Fonts
- Visual Studio Code

## Project Structure
- index.html – Main structure of the application.
- style.css – Visual design and styling.
- README.md – Project documentation.

